  "etymologyNotes": [
    {
      "s": "makemeahanzi",
      "t": "Harvesting 刂 grain 禾"
    },
    {
      "s": "dong_chinese",
      "t": "Depicts harvesting grain (禾) with a blade (刂). Harvest was the main source of profit in agricultural societies."
    },
    {
      "s": "shuowen_jiezi",
      "t": "銛也。从刀。和然後利，从和省。《易》曰：“利者，義之和也。”",
      "w": 1
    },
    {
      "s": "wiktionary",
      "t": "Ideogrammic compound (會意 /会意): 禾 (“grain”) + 刀 (“knife”) – to reap grain (禾) with a knife (刀). See also the variant 𥝢, which appears on top of the character 黎.\nFrom Proto-Sino-Tibetan *ri:t (“to reap, scrape, shave, cut, sever”) (STEDT, Schuessler, 2007); cognate to Mizo rîit (“to scrap with a hoe”), Gurung [script needed] (wriqba, “to scratch”), Burmese ရိတ် (rit, “to cut, reap, mow shave”)."
    }
  ],
  "shuowen": "銛也。从刀。和然後利，从和省。《易》曰：“利者，義之和也。”",
  "shuowenExplanation": "Gains. Composed with 刀 'knife'. 和然後利，从和省. The Book of Changes says: \"利者，義之和也。\".",
